*   University degree or diploma in Social Sciences, Development Studies or another relevant field;  
*   At least 5 years of relevant working experience in children’s rights, child safeguarding and child protection preferably within the civil society sector;  
*   Strong knowledge and skills in child protection including experience in facilitating trainings by using participatory methodologies;  
*   Strong experience in project cycle management;  
*   Good financial management skills and understanding of budgets;  
*   Experience in child participation and the application of the Nine Basic Requirements for Meaningful and Ethical Children’s Participation;  
*   Experience in children’s online safety issues will be an added value;  
*   Knowledge and experience in crosscutting themes such as disability inclusion, gender, and climate change adaptation  
*   Good analytical and report writing skills;  
*   Demonstrated ability to set and achieve objectives;  
*   proficiency in one or more languages commonly spoken in the project locations is an advantage.;  
*   Strong communication (verbal and writing skills), interpersonal and representational skills;  
*   Flexible and adaptable to dynamic changes and fast-paced work environment;  
*   Ability to work with minimal supervision;  
*   Proficiency in Microsoft Word, Excel and Power Point;  
*   Commitment to Save the Children’s vision, mission and values including accountability, ambition, collaboration, creativity and integrity, and to child rights-based approaches.
**APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS:**
**ONLY QUALIFIED APPLICANTS SHOULD APPLY BY ATTACHING A COVER LETTER AND AN UPDATED CV.**
The closing date for receipt of applications is Wednesday 4th November 2026.
Due to the volume of applications we receive, only shortlisted candidates will be contacted by a member of the HR team.
Save the Children reserves the right to re advertise if suitable applicants are not found.
Save the Children is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer that does not engage in any practices which discriminate against any person employed or seeking employment based on race, colour, religion, gender, national or ethnic origin, age, marital status and we will never ask that you pay for anything as part of the selection process or thereafter
